{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task SE-PE-01 involves grammar-guided node reduction. I need to implement `solve(case)` that:\n\n1. Takes a parse tree with nodes having: id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility\n2. Has `required_symbols` that must always remain represented\n3. Must remove nodes according to specific rules\n\nRules:\n- Never remove root, a required symbol node, or a node with retained children\n- Consider deeper nodes before shallower nodes (process deeper first)\n- Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\n- Use node ID as stable tie-break at equal depth\n- Return sorted retained IDs and actual removal order\n\nLet me think about the algorithm:\n\n1. Build the tree structure\n2. Sort nodes by depth (descending - deeper first), then by node ID as tie-break\n3. For each node in that order:\n   - Skip if not removable\n   - Skip if it's a required symbol\n   - Skip if removing it would leave some required symbol unrepresented\n   - Skip if it has retained children\n   - Otherwise, remove it\n4. Return `retained_node_ids` (sorted) and `removed_node_ids` (in removal order)\n\nWait, let me re-read: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\"\n\nSo the conditions for removal:\n- `removable` must be true\n- The node's symbol is not in required_symbols (or wait - it says \"a required symbol\" meaning the symbol must not be required)\n- The node has no retained children (all children have been removed already)\n- After tentative removal, all required symbols are still represented by at least one retained node\n\nAnd the traversal order: deeper nodes first, with node ID as tie-break at equal depth.\n\nLet me trace through case 000:\n\nNodes:\n- root: depth=0, symbol=root, removable=false\n- n1: depth=1, symbol=s1, removable=false\n- n2: depth=1, symbol=s2, removable=true\n- n3: depth=1, symbol=s0, removable=false\n- n4: depth=2, symbol=s1, removable=true, parent=n2\n- n5: depth=2, symbol=s2, removable=false, parent=n3\n- n6: depth=2, symbol=s0, removable=true, parent=n1\n\nrequired_symbols: [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n\nDepth order (descending), then by ID:\n- depth=2: n4, n5, n6\n- depth=1: n1, n2, n3\n- depth=0: root\n\nProcess n4 (depth=2, symbol=s1, removable=true, parent=n2):\n- removable: true\n- symbol s1 is required\n- If we remove n4, we need s1 still represented. n1 has symbol s1 and is retained. So required symbols would still be present.\n- n4 has no children\n- BUT wait: \"Never remove... a required symbol\" - does this mean a node whose symbol is in required_symbols? Or a node that IS the required root?\n\nLooking at the description: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\"\n\nI think \"a required symbol\" means a node whose symbol is listed in required_symbols. But that would mean n1 (symbol=s1) cannot be removed even if removable=false (which it isn't anyway). But also n4 has symbol=s1 which is required...\n\nHmm, but then \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\" - this seems redundant if we can never remove a node with a required symbol.\n\nWait, let me re-read: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\"\n\nI think \"a required symbol\" here might mean a node that is the SOLE remaining representative of a required symbol. That aligns better with \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\"\n\nActually, I think the two rules together mean:\n1. Never remove a node if doing so would leave a required symbol with no representative\n2. \"Never remove the root\" is a specific case (root is always retained regardless)\n\nThe \"a required symbol\" part is perhaps poorly worded and means \"a node whose symbol is required AND is the last such node\". But actually that's just the tentative removal rule.\n\nOR: maybe \"required symbol\" refers to nodes where `removable=false`? No, that's the `removable` field.\n\nLet me re-read more carefully: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\"\n\nI think this literally means:\n- Never remove the root node\n- Never remove a node whose `symbol` is in `required_symbols`\n- Never remove a node that has retained children\n\nThen \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\" is an additional check.\n\nBut wait, if we never remove nodes with required symbols, and required_symbols includes \"s1\", then n4 (symbol=s1) can never be removed. That seems overly restrictive.\n\nHmm, let me look at the fixture data again. In case 000, required_symbols = [\"root\", \"s1\"].\n\nIf n4 (symbol=s1) can never be removed because s1 is required, then:\n- n4: not removable (required symbol)\n- n5: not removable (removable=false)\n- n6: removable=true, symbol=s0 (not required), no children → can we remove?\n  - If we remove n6, are all required symbols still represented?\n  - root: represented by \"root\" node ✓\n  - s1: represented by n1 and n4 ✓\n  - Yes, remove n6\n\nThen at depth 1:\n- n1: removable=false → skip\n- n2: removable=true, symbol=s2 (not required), has child n4 (retained) → has retained children, skip\n- n3: removable=false → skip\n\nResult:\n- removed: [n6]\n- retained: [root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5]\n\nBut wait, this interpretation means nodes with required symbols can NEVER be removed (even if there are multiple nodes with that symbol). That seems too strict.\n\nLet me reconsider. Maybe \"a required symbol\" means a node that is REQUIRED to be present - i.e., a node where removing it would violate the required_symbols constraint. This ties directly to the tentative removal check.\n\nSo the rules might be:\n1. Skip if `removable=false`\n2. Skip if it has retained children\n3. Tentatively remove if all required symbols still represented after removal\n\nAnd \"Never remove the root\" is subsumed by rule 1 (root has removable=false) and by the required_symbols check (root is in required_symbols).\n\nActually I think this is the correct interpretation. The three conditions are really:\n1. Must be `removable=true`\n2. Must have no retained children\n3. After removal, all required symbols must still have at least one retained node\n\nLet me re-trace case 000 with this interpretation:\n\nOrder: n4, n5, n6 (depth 2), then n1, n2, n3 (depth 1), then root (depth 0)\n\nn4 (depth=2, symbol=s1, removable=true):\n- removable: yes\n- no children\n- If removed, s1 represented by n1 → still OK\n- required symbols after removal: root→root node ✓, s1→n1 ✓\n- REMOVE n4\n\nn5 (depth=2, symbol=s2, removable=false):\n- not removable → SKIP\n\nn6 (depth=2, symbol=s0, removable=true):\n- removable: yes  \n- no children\n- required symbols after removal: root→root ✓, s1→n1 (n4 already removed) ✓\n- REMOVE n6\n\nNow depth 1: n1, n2, n3\n\nn1 (depth=1, symbol=s1, removable=false):\n- not removable → SKIP\n\nn2 (depth=1, symbol=s2, removable=true):\n- removable: yes\n- children: n4 (removed) → no retained children\n- If removed, required symbols: root→root ✓, s1→n1 ✓\n- REMOVE n2\n\nn3 (depth=1, symbol=s0, removable=false):\n- not removable → SKIP\n\nroot (depth=0, removable=false):\n- not removable → SKIP\n\nResult:\n- removed_node_ids: [n4, n6, n2] (in removal order)\n- retained_node_ids: sorted [n1, n3, n5, root]\n\nThat makes more sense with the algorithm.\n\nNow let me think about the \"retained children\" check more carefully. When we process n2, n4 has already been removed, so n2 has no retained children. That's why n2 can be removed.\n\nThe order within depth 2 is n4, n5, n6 (alphabetical/lexicographic). Let me verify: \"n4\" \u003c \"n5\" \u003c \"n6\" lexicographically? Yes.\n\nActually, \"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth.\" So at equal depth, sort by node ID. Node IDs are strings, so lexicographic order: n4 \u003c n5 \u003c n6. ✓\n\nNow let me implement this:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Validate required fields\n    for node in nodes:\n        for field in [\"id\", \"parent\", \"symbol\", \"depth\", \"removable\", \"utility\"]:\n            if field not in node:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Missing field {field} in node\")\n    \n    # Build structures\n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    \n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            if n[\"parent\"] not in node_map:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Parent {n['parent']} not found\")\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Track retained status\n    retained = {n[\"id\"]: True for n in nodes}\n    \n    # Sort: deeper first, then by node ID\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    removed_order = []\n    \n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        \n        # Must be removable\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Must have no retained children\n        if any(retained[c] for c in children[nid]):\n            continue\n        \n        # Tentatively remove: check if all required symbols still represented\n        # Current symbol counts among retained nodes (excluding this node)\n        symbol_counts = {}\n        for n in nodes:\n            if retained[n[\"id\"]] and n[\"id\"] != nid:\n                sym = n[\"symbol\"]\n                symbol_counts[sym] = symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) + 1\n        \n        all_required_present = all(symbol_counts.get(sym, 0) \u003e 0 for sym in required_symbols)\n        \n        if all_required_present:\n            retained[nid] = False\n            removed_order.append(nid)\n    \n    retained_ids = sorted(nid for nid, r in retained.items() if r)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_ids\n    }\n```\n\nWait, the symbol count check is O(n) per node, which is fine for small trees. But let me optimize slightly by maintaining a count map:\n\nActually let me think about whether my logic is correct. The check \"all required symbols remain represented\" should count nodes that are still retained (after previous removals) excluding the current node being tentatively removed.\n\nMy implementation does:\n```python\nsymbol_counts = {}\nfor n in nodes:\n    if retained[n[\"id\"]] and n[\"id\"] != nid:\n        ...\n```\n\nThis counts retained nodes excluding the current one. That's correct.\n\nLet me also verify the sort order for the \"retained_node_ids\" return - it says \"Return sorted retained IDs\". Sorted lexicographically? Let me check the schema - it just says array of strings. I'll assume lexicographic sort for consistency.\n\nLet me trace through case 001 to verify:\n\nNodes:\n- root: depth=0, removable=false, symbol=root\n- n1: depth=1, symbol=s1, removable=false\n- n2: depth=1, symbol=s2, removable=true\n- n3: depth=1, symbol=s0, removable=false\n- n4: depth=2, symbol=s1, removable=true, parent=n2\n- n5: depth=2, symbol=s2, removable=false, parent=n3\n- n6: depth=2, symbol=s0, removable=true, parent=n1\n\nrequired_symbols: [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n\nSorted order: n4, n5, n6, n1, n2, n3, root\n\nn4 (removable=true, no children):\n- After removal: root→root ✓, s1→n1 ✓\n- REMOVE n4\n\nn5 (removable=false): SKIP\n\nn6 (removable=true, no children):\n- After removal: root→root ✓, s1→n1 (n4 removed) ✓\n- REMOVE n6\n\nn1 (removable=false): SKIP\n\nn2 (removable=true, children=[n4] but n4 removed → no retained children):\n- After removal: root→root ✓, s1→n1 ✓\n- REMOVE n2\n\nn3 (removable=false): SKIP\n\nroot (removable=false): SKIP\n\nResult:\n- removed: [n4, n6, n2]\n- retained: [n1, n3, n5, root] sorted\n\nSame as case 000! That makes sense given the same structure.\n\nCase 002 would also have the same result since the structure is the same.\n\nLet me now write the clean implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Validate\n    if not isinstance(nodes, list) or len(nodes) == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"nodes must be a non-empty list\")\n    if not isinstance(case[\"required_symbols\"], list):\n        raise ValueError(\"required_symbols must be a list\")\n    \n    for node in nodes:\n        for field in [\"id\", \"parent\", \"symbol\", \"depth\", \"removable\", \"utility\"]:\n            if field not in node:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Node missing required field: {field}\")\n    \n    node_ids = {n[\"id\"] for n in nodes}\n    \n    # Build children map\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            if n[\"parent\"] not in node_ids:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Parent ID {n['parent']} not found in nodes\")\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Track which nodes are currently retained\n    retained = {n[\"id\"]: True for n in nodes}\n    \n    # Count of retained nodes per symbol\n    symbol_retained_count = {}\n    for n in nodes:\n        sym = n[\"symbol\"]\n        symbol_retained_count[sym] = symbol_retained_count.get(sym, 0) + 1\n    \n    # Sort: deeper first, then by node ID (lexicographic) as tie-break\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    removed_order = []\n    \n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        \n        # Must be removable\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Must have no retained children\n        if any(retained[c] for c in children[nid]):\n            continue\n        \n        # Check: if removed, do all required symbols remain represented?\n        sym = node[\"symbol\"]\n        if sym in required_symbols and symbol_retained_count.get(sym, 0) \u003c= 1:\n            # This is the last node with this required symbol\n            continue\n        \n        # Check all required symbols still represented after removal\n        # Since only this node's symbol count decreases, only need to check this symbol\n        # But if sym is not required, no issue\n        # If sym is required, we already checked above\n        # Actually this handles it - proceed with removal\n        \n        # Remove\n        retained[nid] = False\n        symbol_retained_count[sym] = symbol_retained_count.get(sym, 1) - 1\n        removed_order.append(nid)\n    \n    retained_ids = sorted(nid for nid, r in retained.items() if r)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_ids\n    }\n```\n\nWait, the optimization here is that removing a node only affects its own symbol count. So we only need to check if `node.symbol` is in `required_symbols` and if this is the last node with that symbol. That's more efficient.\n\nLet me verify this logic:\n- If node.symbol is NOT in required_symbols: can remove (no required symbol constraint violated)\n- If node.symbol IS in required_symbols: can remove only if count \u003e 1 (at least one other node retains this symbol)\n\nThis is equivalent to checking \"all required symbols remain represented after removal\" because removing one node can only affect the count for its own symbol.\n\nLet me double-check case 000:\n\nn4 (symbol=s1, required): symbol_retained_count[s1] = 2 (n1 and n4) → count \u003e 1 → CAN remove\nAfter removal: symbol_retained_count[s1] = 1\n\nn5: not removable, skip\n\nn6 (symbol=s0, not required): can remove\nAfter removal: symbol_retained_count[s0] = 1 (n3)\n\nn1: not removable, skip\n\nn2 (symbol=s2, not required): \n- Has children: n4 (retained=False) → no retained children → can proceed\n- s2 not required → can remove\nAfter removal: symbol_retained_count[s2] = 1 (n5)\n\nn3: not removable, skip\nroot: not removable, skip\n\nremoved: [n4, n6, n2]\nretained: [root, n1, n3, n5] → sorted: [n1, n3, n5, root]\n\nLooks correct!\n\nNow let me finalize the code and format it as the required JSON output.\n\nThe output must be:\n```json\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    ...\"}\n```\n\nLet me write the final clean implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n\n    # Validate structure\n    if not isinstance(nodes, list) or not nodes:\n        raise ValueError(\"nodes must be a non-empty list\")\n    if not isinstance(case[\"required_symbols\"], list):\n        raise ValueError(\"required_symbols must be a list\")\n\n    for node in nodes:\n        for field in (\"id\", \"parent\", \"symbol\", \"depth\", \"removable\", \"utility\"):\n            if field not in node:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Node missing required field: {field}\")\n\n    node_ids = {n[\"id\"] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None and n[\"parent\"] not in node_ids:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown parent id: {n['parent']}\")\n\n    # Build children map\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n\n    # Retained status and symbol counts\n    retained = {n[\"id\"]: True for n in nodes}\n    symbol_count = {}\n    for n in nodes:\n        symbol_count[n[\"symbol\"]] = symbol_count.get(n[\"symbol\"], 0) + 1\n\n    # Process deeper nodes first; stable tie-break by node ID (lexicographic)\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n\n    removed_order = []\n\n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n\n        # Skip non-removable nodes\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n\n        # Skip if node has retained children\n        if any(retained[c] for c in children[nid]):\n            continue\n\n        # Skip if this is the last retained node carrying a required symbol\n        sym = node[\"symbol\"]\n        if sym in required_symbols and symbol_count.get(sym, 0) \u003c= 1:\n            continue\n\n        # Remove node\n        retained[nid] = False\n        symbol_count[sym] -= 1\n        removed_order.append(nid)\n\n    retained_ids = sorted(nid for nid, r in retained.items() if r)\n\n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_ids,\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks correct and clean. Now I need to format it as a JSON string properly, escaping newlines, quotes, and backslashes.\n\nLet me write the JSON output carefully.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    required_symbols = set(case[\\\"required_symbols\\\"])\\n\\n    # Validate structure\\n    if not isinstance(nodes, list) or not nodes:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"nodes must be a non-empty list\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(case[\\\"required_symbols\\\"], list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"required_symbols must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        for field in (\\\"id\\\", \\\"parent\\\", \\\"symbol\\\", \\\"depth\\\", \\\"removable\\\", \\\"utility\\\"):\\n            if field not in node:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Node missing required field: {field}\\\")\\n\\n    node_ids = {n[\\\"id\\\"] for n in nodes}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n[\\\"parent\\\"] is not None and n[\\\"parent\\\"] not in node_ids:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Unknown parent id: {n['parent']}\\\")\\n\\n    # Build children map\\n    children = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: [] for n in nodes}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n[\\\"parent\\\"] is not None:\\n            children[n[\\\"parent\\\"]].append(n[\\\"id\\\"])\\n\\n    # Track retained status and per-symbol retained counts\\n    retained = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: True for n in nodes}\\n    symbol_count = {}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        symbol_count[n[\\\"symbol\\\"]] = symbol_count.get(n[\\\"symbol\\\"], 0) + 1\\n\\n    # Process deeper nodes first; stable tie-break by node ID (lexicographic)\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\\\"depth\\\"], n[\\\"id\\\"]))\\n\\n    removed_order = []\\n\\n    for node in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = node[\\\"id\\\"]\\n\\n        # Skip non-removable nodes\\n        if not node[\\\"removable\\\"]:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Skip if node has any retained children\\n        if any(retained[c] for c in children[nid]):\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Skip if removing this node would drop a required symbol to zero\\n        sym = node[\\\"symbol\\\"]\\n        if sym in required_symbols and symbol_count.get(sym, 0) \u003c= 1:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Perform removal\\n        retained[nid] = False\\n        symbol_count[sym] -= 1\\n        removed_order.append(nid)\\n\\n    retained_ids = sorted(nid for nid, r in retained.items() if r)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"removed_node_ids\\\": removed_order,\\n        \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": retained_ids,\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_013SbQO6uL6q8BLkseJniJD1","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2505,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":85,"output_tokens":5755,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5085},"service_tier":"standard"}}